            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for good-hearted, then the Gujarati for to soften with pity."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ભોળું",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ભોળું — bhoḷũ — \"innocent; trusting\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "નાનું બાળક ભોળું હોય છે. nānũ bāḷak bhoḷũ hoy che. A small child is trusting."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ભોળું (bhoḷũ) goes back to a reconstructed bhulla-, \"defective\"; CDIAL lists the Gujarati word, \"foolish, credulous\" (CDIAL 9539), and today it is mostly the innocence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
